  "narrative": {
    "intro": "California's total federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date are $524M. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $251M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $205M in the same period. The state recorded 4,436 awards with an average award size of $118K. Obligations are down 99.1% year over year. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations at $147M. CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY is the largest vendor by obligations at $128M, followed by IMPULSE SPACE, INC. at $37.1M and BECKMAN COULTER, INC at $27.4M. FY22 through FY26 annual obligations were $57.5B, $61.5B, $61.7B, $62B, and $57.5B respectively, highlighting a much larger historical scale compared with the FY2027 to date figure. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers in California in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer at $251M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the second-largest buyer at $205M. The Department of Justice, General Services Administration, and Department of the Interior follow with $17.8M, $17M, and $13.2M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries dominate California federal contracting in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY is the top vendor at $128M. IMPULSE SPACE, INC., and BECKMAN COULTER, INC are the next largest vendors at $37.1M and $27.4M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top industry at $147M, followed by Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing at $46M and Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $43.6M."
      }
    ]
